@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] web-no-style-blocks
A Vue SFC MUST NOT have a `<style>` block, scoped or not. Elements are styled with UnoCSS
utilities in the template; markup the template cannot reach gets a shortcut in
`uno.config.ts` (AGENTS.md).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] web-wears-the-phone-kit
The web is drawn from the phone's sources: tokens, `Lu` icons and fonts come from the
generated files in `src/design`, and `src/components/kit/` holds the phone's pieces.
The standalone web MUST use the Android mobile layout at every host width, centered
in a portrait viewport with blank side padding on wide screens. Every piece is the
phone's piece, with no link-out arrows or AI sparkles. Tavi explicitly replaced the
wide-layout allowance with 1-to-1 Android parity on 6 Nov 2026 (rule 106).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] web-is-static
The public site builds as a static SPA with no backend: nothing is proxied through a
server we run, and no secret is kept server-side. GitHub and model access use keys the
user supplies (architecture, Invariants).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] web-strings-through-i18n
Every user-facing string goes through vue-i18n, and the web locales are the source the
phone's strings are copied from (architecture, UI conventions).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] web-no-preview-host-in-public-comments
A link in a comment posted to GitHub uses the hardcoded `https://pulls.review` origin; a
preview host MUST NOT leak into a public comment (architecture, Sharing).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] web-pagination-awaits-active-page
Concurrent pagination consumers MUST await the active page request, and MUST NOT spin
without waiting for network progress. A superseded continuation MUST NOT replace the
new list or its error state (repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding #1).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] web-group-navigation-uses-own-root
File-tree and parent-group navigation MUST find their targets in the group's owning
Document or ShadowRoot, including recursively rendered embedded groups
(repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding #15).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] web-chat-start-is-busy
A pending server chat start MUST reserve the busy state before awaiting the RPC.
Detaching MUST prevent its late response from restarting a follower; stopping during
startup MUST cancel the returned task without following it. Startup failure MUST
release the busy state (repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding #16).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] web-discovery-preserves-current-analysis
Shared-analysis discovery MUST check the current AI result after comments arrive and
offer a candidate instead of replacing a locally generated result. Dismissed or
superseded discovery MUST NOT apply results or repopulate candidates
(repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding #17).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] web-public-site-untracked
Only the build our server serves (`PR_LOCAL`) tracks usage, through `src/local/analytics.ts`
and `POST /api/events`. The public pulls.review site MUST NOT send analytics anywhere until
Tavi decides it should (plan "Pulls analytics on our own server", Open questions).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-mobile-viewport-owns-every-layer
The standalone web MUST render pages, fixed controls, sheets, menus and toasts in the
same portrait viewport. Wide host windows MUST NOT activate desktop layouts inside
that viewport. Narrow phone windows MUST fill the available width. Browser links,
deep links, reload, Back and Forward MUST continue to address the visible route.
Source: Tavi's 6 Nov 2026 request for the web to feel like Android with blank side padding.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-inbox-matches-android
The standalone home MUST use Android's Inbox and Tours capsule, Waiting on you,
Authored and All filters, grouped rows, bottom search pill and adjacent sort button.
Row swipes MUST commit only after horizontal intent; vertical scrolling MUST NOT
open or archive a row. Archiving MUST offer Undo and remain local to the inbox.
Source: Tavi's 6 Nov 2026 1-to-1 Android request and shared HomeScreen.kt/Triage.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] web-feedback-uses-android-recipes
Web control sounds MUST use Android's Cuelume recipe asset, materials, role-based
cues and emphasis shaping. Secondary controls MUST use subtle emphasis. Text entry
and opening, closing or navigating a page by themselves MUST remain silent. Sound
MUST play only on committed activation; disabling sound MUST fade current voices.
Audio unavailability MUST NOT prevent an action. Source: Tavi's 6 Nov 2026 request
for the same sound as Android and DESIGN.md rules 109, 120 and 125.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-review-matches-android-frame
The standalone pull request MUST use Android's fixed Overview, Changes and Tour
capsule. Changes MUST show one selected file at a time, retain review marks and
comments, and permit split layout in portrait. Overview MUST retain access to
conversation, commits, checks, files and existing review/state actions through sheets.
Tours MUST use the existing tour cache and server tasks, reserve busy state before
starting a task, and detach without cancelling when the page leaves. Source:
Tavi's 6 Nov 2026 1-to-1 Android request and shared ReviewScreen.kt/PrDiffScreen.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-sheets-use-phone-interactions
Standalone dialogs MUST use the phone's paper sheet, rounded top corners, grabber,
press feedback and reduced-motion preference. Only the topmost sheet MAY handle
keyboard dismissal or trap focus; background scrolling MUST stay locked until the
last sheet closes, and closing a sheet MUST restore focus. Source: Tavi's 6 Nov
2026 Android parity request and DESIGN.md rules 78, 82 and 108.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] web-parity-preserves-authority
The mobile web presentation MUST retain the existing static-client and local-RPC
boundaries. The static client MUST use only viewer-supplied GitHub authority; local
inbox questions and tours MUST use existing typed task APIs. The mobile frame MUST
NOT grant browser access to posted diffs or expose server-held credentials. Source:
Tavi's 6 Nov 2026 request to match Android with minimal backend changes; root
posted-diffs-not-on-the-web and github-token-stays-on-server contracts.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] web-tour-diagrams-use-native-renderer
Tour diagrams MUST use the bundled Pele renderer Android uses and the shared phone
palette. Rendering MUST disable links and images and bound source and SVG sizes.
Executable SVG elements, event handlers and remote resource references MUST NOT
reach the document. Source: Tavi's 6 Nov 2026 Android parity request and the native
PeleSvg.kt rendering boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-stacks-use-native-rows
Inbox stacks MUST collapse into Android's outlined stack row with aggregate facts and
open their layers on activation. Source: Tavi's 7 Nov 2026 request for a second full
1-to-1 pass; PullRowContent.kt and InboxStacks.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-tours-retain-reading-progress
Saved tours MUST use the native progress tile and retain reading progress across
navigation and reload. Source: Tavi's 7 Nov 2026 full Android parity pass; PullRows.kt
and PrTourScreen.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-native-reading-preferences
Settings MUST offer Android's fonts, palettes, code sizes and wrapping, and selected
fonts MUST reach code in shadow DOM. Source: Tavi's 7 Nov 2026 full Android parity
pass; SettingsScreen.kt and Samples.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] web-native-diff-washes
Diff line washes MUST use the native colors without the renderer diluting them.
Source: Tavi's 7 Nov 2026 full Android parity pass; FileDiff.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-commands-match-native
Pulling the Inbox beyond its top MUST open Commands after Android's resisted
threshold while bottom controls stay pinned. Commands MUST use a tall sheet with
plain grouped rows and search; secondary groups MUST initially limit their rows and
allow expansion. Source: Tavi's 7 Nov 2026 full Android parity pass; PullToCommands.kt
and CommandPalette.kt.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] web-ask-pill-follows-native
The Overview and Tour Ask bar MUST rest as Android's compact Ask pill, expand with
focus on activation and collapse when left empty. Tapping the field's padding MUST
focus it. The Tour MUST show Ask only once there is a tour to discuss. Source: Tavi's
7 Nov 2026 full Android parity pass; AskBar.kt, FootBar.kt and PrTourScreen.kt (Q5, Q6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] web-phone-layers-have-real-depth
The search dim MUST cover the page header, the foot bar MUST stay above that dim,
and Tour's pinned section strip MUST cover scrolling cards. These layers MUST use
named Uno shortcuts, since the design preset blocks literal arbitrary z-index
utilities in templates. Source: Tavi's 7 Nov 2026 full Android parity pass; observed
header and card overlap, and PrTourScreen.kt / AskBar.kt (N29).
